{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The policy sets a deliberately high bar for both recall and look-alike rejection. I’m mapping each development class to concrete examples now, with special attention to original-script-only entries and stacked transliteration changes; those are the areas where generic fuzzy matching tends to create unsafe false positives."}}
